<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Axis powers</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Axis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Axis powers were the alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, with other partners, that fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a> joined Germany in 1940, but suffered heavy defeats in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. Italy's defeat led to the loss of all its colonies and the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/axis-powers.jpg" alt="Axis powers" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unbekannter Fotograf (Foto vom 17. Dezember 1940) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Celebration_of_the_Japan-Germany-Italy-Triparite-Pact_(1940)_in_Tokio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Origins</h2><p>The Italian prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> first applied the word axis to the Italo-German relationship in September 1923, writing that the axis of European history was passing through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a>; he was then seeking an alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weimar-republic">Weimar Republic</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. After negotiations between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galeazzo-ciano">Galeazzo Ciano</a> and Ulrich von Hassell, Ciano and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konstantin-von-neurath">Konstantin von Neurath</a> signed a Nine-Point Protocol in 1936, and on 1 November Mussolini announced a Rome-Berlin axis.</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anti-comintern-pact">Anti-Comintern Pact</a>, an anti-communist treaty between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, was ratified in November 1936. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> joined it in 1937, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1939. The Rome-Berlin Axis became a military alliance under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-steel">Pact of Steel</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact">Tripartite Pact</a> of 1940 formally integrated the military aims of Germany, Italy and Japan.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">History</h2><p>Six other countries signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact">Tripartite Pact</a>. Hungary was the first, on 20 November 1940, under Regent Miklós Horthy. Slovakia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, the Independent State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> also took part in Axis military operations, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>'s signatory government was overthrown in a coup days after it signed, and the membership was reversed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> set up puppet governments in occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, merged on 29 March 1940 into the Reorganized National Government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jingwei">Wang Jingwei</a>, which had no real power. A State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> was formed on 1 August 1943 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ba-maw">Ba Maw</a>.</p><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a> on 7 December 1941, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-pact">Tripartite Pact</a> required <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to help only if Japan were attacked, yet Hitler ordered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichstag">Reichstag</a> to declare war on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and Italy also declared war. Ian Kershaw suggests this was a serious blunder, since it let the United States join the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> without limitation. At its zenith in 1942 the Axis presided over large parts of Europe, North Africa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, through occupation, annexation or puppet states. It ended with its defeat in 1945.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Organisation and way of life</h2><p>The Axis's primary goal was territorial expansion at the expense of neighbours, and it championed variants of fascism, militarism, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conservatism">conservatism</a> and autarky. Unlike the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>, there were no three-way summit meetings, cooperation was minimal, and at times the interests of the major powers were at variance. The Axis population in 1938 was 258.9 million, against 689.7 million for the Allies excluding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Italy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> lacked industrial capacity, and their mobilisation remained low even by 1943.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Axis powers” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Spain remained formally non-belligerent or neutral in that war but in practice supported the <b>Axis</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/francoist-spain">Francoist Spain · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Axis powers</b> invaded and occupied Yugoslavia in 1941.</blockquote><a href="/empire/independent-state-of-croatia">Independent State of Croatia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In North Africa, Italian forces advanced into Egypt in 1940 but were routed during the British counter-offensive that winter, and after German intervention the <b>Axis</b> was decisively defeated at the Second Battle of El Alamein in 1942.</blockquote><a href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>During the <b>Axis</b> occupation of 1941–44, when famine killed tens of thousands in Athens and Piraeus and most of the Jews of Thessaloniki were deported to Auschwitz in 1943, the king and government were in exile, and the communist-led resistance of EAM-ELAS opposed their return.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Through the First Vienna Award it regained southern Czechoslovakia, then occupied the Carpatho-Ukraine, and through the Second Vienna Award it gained Northern Transylvania, before joining the <b>Axis powers</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1920-1946">Kingdom of Hungary (1920-1946) · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Second World War Romania fought with the <b>Axis</b> until King Michael's Coup of 1944 brought it over to the Allies.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-romania">Kingdom of Romania · Military</a></li></ul></section>
